  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "A data set has a mean $\\overset{\u2015}{x}=-0.3$ and a standard deviation $\\sigma =0.5.$ An observation of the data set has a $z$-score $z=1.4.$ Find the value $x$ of this observation.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{\u2015}{x}=-0.3,$ $z=1.4,$ and $\\sigma =0.5$ into the formula and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ x & =-0.3+1.4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\ x & =-0.3+0.7 \\\\ x & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
